{{Wireless adapter |brand=I-O DATA |model=WN-AC433 |revision=UK |upc= |ean=4957180107608 |asin=B00C58G5Z4;JP; |price= |est_release_date=07/2013 |fcc_date= |manuf_country= |is_manuf=No |manuf=Edimax |manuf_model= |manuf_rev= |availability=Japan only |if=USB |if_bus_version=2.0 |if_connector_type=Male A |form_factor=micro dongle |vendor_id=04bb |device_id=0951 |subvendor_id= |subdevice_id= |id_string= |fcc_id= |ic_id= |chip1_brand=MediaTek |chip1_model=MT7610U |addl_chips= |accessible_UART=No |flags= |ant_conn= |802dot11_protocols=abgn+ac |txchains=1 |rxchains=1 |sstreams=1 |oui= |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} {{ProductPage|http://www.iodata.jp/product/network/adp/wn-ac433u/}} (JP) :{{SupportPage|http://www.iodata.jp/product/network/adp/wn-ac433u/support.htm}}
This device is found in the driver set for '''Sitecom''''s MT7610U dongle :- it is also presumed to be using [[MediaTek MT7610U]].
===Additional external links=== *[http://bbs.kakaku.com/bbs/K0000487849/SortID=16151076/ImageID=1560173/ Board shot on '''Kakaku'''] :"1244-00000116-50Z" is silkscreened on the board. This is an '''Edimax''' manufactured device.
